    "bio": "a Representative from Michigan; born in St. Joseph, Berrien County, Mich., April 23, 1953; graduated from the Shattuck School, Fairbault, Minn., 1971; B.A., University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, Mich., 1975; staff, United States Representative David Stockman of Michigan, 1976-1980; staff, Office of Management and Budget, 1981-1985; elected as a Republican to the One Hundredth and to the seventeen succeeding Congresses (January 3, 1987-January 3, 2023); chair, Committee on Energy and Commerce (One Hundred Twelfth through One Hundred Fourteenth Congresses); was not a candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Eighteenth Congress in 2022.",
